  "description": "YIJWUJ10 crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H80 Nd4 O33 Si16 6-,10(C2 H6 O1),8(H2 O1),6(Na1 1+). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd1B (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2B (Nd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.650-5.290 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.49-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Na6{[(C6H5SiO2)8]2Nd4(μ4-O)}·10EtOH·8H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
